GoldLink's change to melonDS (UC12): the attached objects drawn at the phase within a pixel the
player has at rest.

Patch 0022 drew them with the reference at a fixed phase within a pixel, so at rest the player's
picture was up to half a pixel off the world's (the user's play test: the player's pixels not
lined up with the world's even standing still). The phase is now the one the reference has at a
scene whose camera stands where the last scene's did (at rest): there the player is drawn where
the DS draws them, on the world's pixels, and the window shows the two pictures (patch 0026) with
no offset; moving, every picture of them has the same pixels, slid by their fraction. And each
attached object at its true offset from the reference (not whole pixels: the player was drawn half
a pixel off the DS's place when the reference was their follower or shadow), kept while it changes
by no more than the arithmetic's noise.

Applied by build.rs to a copy of the submodule (which stays at upstream).

